cements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-08T12:27:46-07:00","id":1138665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1138582-gilgul-rite-changed?p=1138662#post1138662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, it's not actually a rite most player characters at my games have been EAGER to use. It's something highly controversial in-universe.<br /> <br /> Certainly, Heylel didn't deserve to have it done to him.<br /> <br /> I don't see why Spirit 5 users would &quot;abuse&quot; it in-game.</div> </div> </div> </div>If all a nephandus needed was Spirit 5 to effectively shatter the souls of their enemies, with the techniques reserved for them no less, you can bet it would be abused.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-08T12:33:43-07:00","id":1138669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1138582-gilgul-rite-changed?p=1138665#post1138665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If all a nephandus needed was Spirit 5 to effectively shatter the souls of their enemies, with the techniques reserved for them no less, you can bet it would be abused.</div> </div> </div> </div>While Nephandi are bad people, I don't think we've ever seen any desire to destroy souls from them since they traditionally feed those to their masters when they don't corrupt people.<br /> <br /> The Technocracy might want to get rid of all avatars.<br /> <br /> Thankfully, the people who would in the Progenitors are the ones least equipped to understand spirit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-08T13:30:42-07:00","id":1138692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1138582-gilgul-rite-changed?p=1138669#post1138669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While Nephandi are bad people, I don't think we've ever seen any desire to destroy souls from them since they traditionally feed those to their masters when they don't corrupt people.<br /> <br /> The Technocracy might want to get rid of all avatars.<br /> <br /> Thankfully, the people who would in the Progenitors are the ones least equipped to understand spirit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not even them. Technocracy values the Genius, even those that have understanding of what it really is. They don't fear Geniuses reappearing because they know that a new Genius can be recuited and Traditionalist mages can be converted to the good cause (trough judicious use of Conditioning). I can imagine they doing Gilgul to specially stubborn Traditional Avatars that try to push the Technocrat trough wrong paths, but only if the mage can't keep it under control (like it happens with Inverted Avatars). Now, if Conditioning Avatars was possible-in a similar but Techno-friendly way as what Nephandi do, THAT would be the dream of any NWO DimSci specialist. Technocracy want's Control, not destruction, they only kill what they can't control.<br /> <br /> And as for Nephandi: Gilgul deprives the Dark masters from a perfectly good soul to invert (Bad for their goals) andisn't a good combat spell (too hard to cast). I can't imagine a common situation where Nephandi would want to cast it, if a Mage refused to be corrupted, you can always kill the mage and try again in the next life. <br /> <br /> I don't think Spirit 5 it's &quot;too little&quot;. It's a spell that has little practical use (bad for combat because it's hard, your Avatar hates you if you use it, Always Vulgar, grant's you bad resonance, Mages hate you for using it...) other than assuring that your enemy isn't going to pass foggy memories of your character to a new incarnation (usually mages don't remember much, but there are exeptions).<br /> <br /> That being said, I know exactly who would have wanted to abuse it:<i> Euthanatos and Akashicks.</i><br /> During the Himalaya war Avatars reincarnating with memories of past battles were a real problem, I imagine that killing Avatars would have been very practical. Now, they both are very adamant against the idea of breaking reincarnation by brute force, but surely at least one Master tought about it. The secret experimets to develop this &quot;ultimate weapon&quot; could make interesting story hook.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 09-08-2017, 04:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-09T06:39:01-07:00","id":1138873,"title":"","content":"Wouldn't multiple mages of the same paradigm and practice just cast it together? Much more plausible that you could get four Hermetic masters together rather than one who's mastered all four spheres.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7356-haldir2012","name":"haldir2012","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-09T06:48:25-07:00","id":1138875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1138582-gilgul-rite-changed?p=1138692#post1138692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That being said, I know exactly who would have wanted to abuse it:<i> Euthanatos and Akashicks.</i><br /> During the Himalaya war Avatars reincarnating with memories of past battles were a real problem, I imagine that killing Avatars would have been very practical. Now, they both are very adamant against the idea of breaking reincarnation by brute force, but surely at least one Master tought about it. The secret experimets to develop this &quot;ultimate weapon&quot; could make interesting story hook.</div> </div> </div> </div>Such a True Mage could perhaps cast a spell to remove and/or cloud specific memories of an Avatar that they expected to reappear. Then there would be no need to go after the entire Avatar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}